Add full lists of ALL added and removed blocks and ALL added and removed items to the infographic so a mapping group can see every change without opening the CLI. This will make the infographic long, which is acceptable (no required aspect ratio); make each table compact (smaller font, tight row height, possibly multi-column) to compensate. Columns at minimum: +/-, block/item name (elide long item paths), position (free-look blocks only; use '--' for normal/ghost blocks per B059 convention). These lists sit below the grouped per-name summaries (B073).

Lane plan (2026-09-11): serial infographic-rendering lane after B069/B070/B068 because all tasks share scene/layout/painter/tests. Decision: place the existing grouped placement summary immediately above new unbounded compact placement tables. Include every added/removed block, baked block, and item; exclude modified placements because the ticket asks for added/removed lists. Show actual position only for free blocks and items; normal/ghost blocks use -- per B059; baked blocks retain their available physical position. Canvas height grows and long item paths are elided.